[**12-8**] 71 yo female came to ER from home w/ intermittent SOB x3 weeks, increasing DOE, and + lower back pain;
   w/u dx'd pt w/ metastatic small cell lung CA, met to liver, thought to be ACTH-secreting tumor; also treated for obstructive pna;
   recently received chemo [**12-12**], [**12-13**], and [**12-14**]; pt developed melanous stool w/ drop in hct, resulting in multiple transfusions [**12-13**] - [**12-15**]; had recently had an EGD [**11-30**] which showed several adenamatous polyps--RBC scan unremarkable;
   transferred to [**Hospital Unit Name 328**] [**12-17**] for repeat EGD; sourse of GIB reportedly not visualized;

[**Name (NI) **] pt vss, o x 2, confused--pt's daughter reportedly states pt gets confused at night; this night pt oriented to person, variable on place; tried to get OOB 3 times, pt had been incontinent those 3 times of urine in the bed, the third time also of stool--abit of black, then brown very soft;
   pt received 2 transfusion of plts from approx. 20:00-22:00;
   23:00 CBC showed continued low hct, ordered for another unit of PRBC's, received from approx. 00:30 to 03:00;
   23:00 plt ct 99, significant increase from pre-transfusion;

bed alarm in use this shift for pt safety, so far effective, no untoward events occurred;
   foley placed at third attempt of pt to get OOB when bed wet w/ incontinence, to assist w/ accurate I/O; urine output volumes showing excellent urine output, light clear yellow--(?auti diuresing?)--also suggests pt not bleeding;

received K+ supplementation overnight, 40 mEq at 20:00, 20 mEq at 00:00 and 02:00; pt did not have difficulty swallowing, HOB put up approx 80 degrees for swallowing of pills;

receiving RISS q 6 hrs FS;

PLAN:
1) likely return to regular floor today [**12-18**], if pt asymptomatic of bleeding
